## 1. Navigation architecture overview

Given your stack & dependencies (`@react-navigation/native`, `@react-navigation/native-stack`, `@react-navigation/bottom-tabs`), a solid structure is:

* **RootStack**

  * Handles:

    * Splash / loading
    * Auth vs Main app
    * Global modals (e.g. Guided Study Session)
* **AuthStack**

  * Login, OTP, etc. (even if not built yet, keep placeholder)
* **MainTabs** (bottom tab navigator)

  * `HomeTab` – dashboard, progress, notifications
  * `ClassesTab` – schedules, live classes, tests
  * `StudyTab` – library, AI study, syllabus
  * `DoubtsTab` – doubts, doubt history, explore doubts
  * `CommunityTab` – peers, groups, gamification
  * `ProfileTab` – profile, settings, help

Each tab is **a stack navigator** so you get deep navigation while keeping the tab bar.

